      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town of Cincinnati was incorporated in February 1875, marking its official start as a municipality.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cincinnati%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Cincinnati began as a coal mining camp, a typical 19th‑century boomtown that drew workers and conflict alike.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cincinnati%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town became a hotbed of union activity, strikes, and occasional violence as miners fought for better conditions.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cincinnati%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 1895, Company E of the Iowa National Guard was called up to quell threats from striking miners in Cincinnati.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cincinnati%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
